=== narrow ===

 draw the awkward markdown


A table whose rows do not all reach the
end:

┌──────┬────────────────┬──────┐
│ tool │ what it does   │ cost │
├──────┼────────────────┼──────┤
│ read │                │      │
├──────┼────────────────┼──────┤
│ grep │ walks the tree │ 4    │
├──────┼────────────────┼──────┤
│ bash │ runs a command │ 40   │
└──────┴────────────────┴──────┘

A narrow table in a wide terminal:

┌───┬───┐
│ a │ b │
├───┼───┤
│ 1 │ 2 │
└───┴───┘

A bare URL the renderer has to find for
itself: https://example.com/plain and
one
in angle brackets
https://example.com/bracketed, which are
not the same thing.

Entities are resolved in prose — AT&T
becomes AT&T — but left alone inside
code, where &amp; and &lt;div&gt; stand
as they are written.
